From: RelicOS <relicos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: odroid_go2: RelicOS default environment with the A/B slot chooser

RelicOS keeps two copies of the system on the card (boot_a/root_a and
boot_b/root_b, GPT partitions 1-4) and updates the one not in use. The
bootloader has to pick one, remember how many times it tried it, and
fall back to the other when it fails -- and that memory has to survive a
bad update, so the logic cannot live in the slots themselves.

Add a text-based default environment, board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/
relicos.env, selected with CONFIG_ENV_SOURCE_FILE="relicos" and run by
CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="run relicos_boot". It is the U-Boot script RAUC
documents for its "uboot" bootloader backend, with this board's names:
BOOT_ORDER lists the slots to try, BOOT_a_LEFT/BOOT_b_LEFT count the
attempts left; the script decrements, saves the environment, and only
then loads the slot's boot.scr (mmc 0:1 or 0:2), exporting
relicos_bootpart, relicos_slot and relicos_root for it. The running
system (or RAUC) sets the count back to 3 once it is up.

Being the default environment, it is what U-Boot uses when the saved
copy on the card is absent or corrupt -- which is the point: the state
lives on the card, the logic in the firmware.

The stock odroid-go2 environment is untouched; the file only adds
relicos_boot.
---
diff --git a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/relicos.env b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/relicos.env
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/relicos.env
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+/*
+ * RelicOS default environment (M25): the A/B slot chooser.
+ *
+ * Compiled into U-Boot through CONFIG_ENV_SOURCE_FILE="relicos" (see
+ * board/r36s/uboot.fragment in the RelicOS tree). This is the DEFAULT
+ * environment, the one U-Boot falls back to when the copy saved on the
+ * card is missing or has a bad CRC. That is deliberate: the card copy
+ * holds only the STATE (BOOT_ORDER, BOOT_a_LEFT, BOOT_b_LEFT); the LOGIC
+ * lives here, in the firmware, where a wrong fw_setenv cannot reach it.
+ * A card whose environment is lost boots "a first, three tries each".
+ *
+ * The scheme is the one RAUC documents for U-Boot (rauc.readthedocs.io,
+ * Integration, Bootloader, U-Boot), with RelicOS names: slots are a and b
+ * like the partitions (boot_a = mmc 0:1, boot_b = mmc 0:2, root_x =
+ * PARTUUID 52454c49-0002-...-000x, pinned in genimage.cfg). The updater
+ * writes into the inactive slot and sets BOOT_ORDER="b a" BOOT_b_LEFT=3;
+ * the running system writes BOOT_<slot>_LEFT=3 back once it is up
+ * (S98bootok; later rauc status mark-good). Every boot attempt costs one
+ * count, taken and SAVED before the attempt, so a kernel that never comes
+ * back has already paid. Three failures move on to the next slot in the
+ * order; no slot left resets the counters and restarts the board.
+ *
+ * The conversion script joins the lines of a variable with spaces, hence
+ * the semicolons: this is one hush line.
+ *
+ * The boot.scr of the chosen slot still does everything else (board id,
+ * device tree, bootargs), reading relicos_bootpart, relicos_slot and
+ * relicos_root from here. A load that fails (a slot with no filesystem,
+ * as boot_b ships) or a source that returns (a boot.scr that never reached
+ * booti) falls through to the next slot in the same boot.
+ */
+
+relicos_boot=
+	test -n "${BOOT_ORDER}" || setenv BOOT_ORDER "a b";
+	test -n "${BOOT_a_LEFT}" || setenv BOOT_a_LEFT 3;
+	test -n "${BOOT_b_LEFT}" || setenv BOOT_b_LEFT 3;
+	for slot in ${BOOT_ORDER}; do
+		if test "${slot}" = a; then
+			setenv relicos_bootpart 1; setenv left ${BOOT_a_LEFT};
+		elif test "${slot}" = b; then
+			setenv relicos_bootpart 2; setenv left ${BOOT_b_LEFT};
+		else
+			setenv left 0;
+		fi;
+		if test ${left} -gt 0; then
+			setexpr left ${left} - 1;
+			setenv BOOT_${slot}_LEFT ${left};
+			setenv relicos_slot ${slot};
+			setenv relicos_root PARTUUID=52454c49-0002-0000-0000-00000000000${slot};
+			echo "RelicOS: slot ${slot}, ${left} attempts left after this one";
+			saveenv;
+			if load mmc 0:${relicos_bootpart} ${scriptaddr} boot.scr; then
+				source ${scriptaddr};
+			fi;
+			echo "RelicOS: slot ${slot} did not boot";
+		fi;
+	done;
+	echo "RelicOS: no slot left to try, resetting the counters";
+	setenv BOOT_a_LEFT 3; setenv BOOT_b_LEFT 3; saveenv;
+	reset
